{"name":"Marvellous","hex":"#6a7fb4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"marvellous","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Exciting wonder or surprise; astonishing; wonderful."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Marvellously (wondrously; very; extremely)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marvellous"}],"entries":[{"title":"Marvellous","blocks":[{"text":"Marvellous is a 90-minute British drama television film first broadcast on BBC Two on 25 September 2014. Directed by Julian Farino and written by Peter Bowker, it is about the life of Neil Baldwin from Westlands, Newcastle-under-Lyme, Staffordshire."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1f/Marvellous_DVD_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marvellous","wikidata":"Q16997400"},{"title":"Marvellous (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Marvellous is an Irish Thoroughbred racehorse who won the Irish 1,000 Guineas at The Curragh by three lengths. She is trained by Aidan O'Brien and owned by Derrick Smith, Susan Magnier and Michael Tabor."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Marvellous_%28horse%29.jpg/330px-Marvellous_%28horse%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marvellous_(horse)","wikidata":"Q17984700"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"marvellous":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/dc/En-gb-marvellous.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/dc/En-gb-marvellous.ogg/En-gb-marvellous.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f8/En-us-marvellous.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","s